      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "I bought a 2KW hybrid system (8 panels) with SLA batteries to suit a 4.5KW system for $16,000.  I had installed 8 panels previously through Genlux, one of 9 companies which had gone into liquidation.   These panels were Blueline Solar and I was very pleased with them.   I received a letter from the Queensland Government on 29th August 2015, advising me that the solar system had been installed with \"a particularly  unsafe model 'Avanco' brand DC isolators, which is part of a product recall.\"   This prompted me to contact you with reference to installers in this area;  Solar Today were advertising in the local paper at that time.   I have received a letter, on 8th October 2015, from Solar Service Care Pty Ltd, advising me that they are the authorised service for Genlux and will assist with any warranty claims, ongoing maintenance and repairs.The installers for Solar Today did an excellent job and I am delighted with this hybrid system.",
